-Studio now owns `.deps\rocm` inside the project. `RUN.bat` performs a one-time migration from an older ROCm install when needed. The hipBLASLt environment is pointed at the architecture-specific `bin\hipblaslt\library\gfx1151` directory, where `TensileLibrary_lazy_gfx1151.*` and gfx1151 code objects live.
+Studio owns `.deps\rocm` inside the project. `BUILD.bat` can seed it from a valid installed Windows gfx1151 ROCm SDK or download the pinned package directly. The hipBLASLt environment is pointed at the architecture-specific `bin\hipblaslt\library\gfx1151` directory, where `TensileLibrary_lazy_gfx1151.*` and gfx1151 code objects live.
+
+## v1.0.8: top-wins verification patch
+
+Compact sampled MTP verification now keeps the authoritative final full-vocabulary target row on the GPU. The next anchor is sampled from the exact Top-256 certificate when that certificate is sufficient; a full-vocabulary D2H transfer happens only on certificate fallback, rejection-frontier handling, snapshots, or an explicit `Logits()` read. This removes the previous unconditional full-row transfer from every successful compact verification cycle without changing target sampling, penalties, seeded RNG consumption, or rollback semantics.
+
+The build keeps the LLVM 23 `gfx1151` W8A8 scheduler-barrier fix already present in the v1.0.6 baseline, rejects a source tree that regresses to unconditional verification-frontier D2H, and removes the hard-coded fallback to `C:\flashfknworkalready` from the ROCm helper.
+
+`BENCHMARK-TOP-WINS.bat` runs a repeatable profiled suite using the Studio's effective sampler/thinking settings, fixed prompt hashes and seeds, and optional long-context ladder. Use the same saved settings for baseline/patched runs; the script refuses A/B comparison when settings or prompt hashes differ.
+
+See `OPTIMIZATION-PASS-v1.0.8.md` for the source evidence and cross-project audit.
 
